  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $f$ be a differentiable function satisfying $f\\prime(x)=f\\prime(-x)$ for all $x$. Then",
  "options": {
    "A": "$f$ is an odd function",
    "B": "$f(x)+f(-x)=2f(0)$ for all $x$",
    "C": "$\\frac12 f(x)+\\frac12 f(y)=f\\left(\\frac{x+y}{2}\\right)$ for all $x,y$",
    "D": "If $f(1)=f(2)$, then $f(-1)=f(-2)$"
  },
  "answer": "B,D",
